<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The other half of tests.runsettings: this one runs ONLY the slow cases (NUnit category
  "ReleaseOnly": the polymer models, the polymerization reactor and the dynamic column runs), which
  is what to do before cutting a release. About 50 minutes, 14 cases.

      dotnet test tests\DWSIM.FluentAPI.Tests /settings:tests\releaseonly.runsettings

  Selecting the group with a test filter on the command line does NOT work: a filter given there is
  combined with the one in tests.runsettings (TestCategory!=ReleaseOnly), the intersection is empty,
  and the run reports success having executed nothing. Overriding RunConfiguration.TestCaseFilter
  through the run settings arguments does not win over the project's settings file either. Replacing
  the settings file, as above, is what selects the group. Check the case count on the summary line.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <TestCaseFilter>TestCategory=ReleaseOnly</TestCaseFilter>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
